      <tei:div type="notes">
        <tei:p>“Für Chanuka” was translated/adapted by Yehoshua Heshil Miro and published in his anthology of teḥinot, בית יעקב (Beit Yaaqov) <tei:hi rend="italic">Allgemeines Gebetbuch für gebildete Frauen mosaicher Religion</tei:hi>. It first appears in the 1829 edition, תחנות <tei:hi rend="italic">Teḥinot ein Gebetbuch für gebildete Frauenzimmer mosaicher Religion</tei:hi> as teḥinah No54 on pp. 79-81. In the 1835 edition, it appears as teḥinah No56 pp. 101-103. In the 1842 edition, it appears as teḥinah No59 on pp. 106-108.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>We welcome corrections and improvements. The transcription of the German from Latin script in Fraktur type provided machine-readable text for a machine translation by DeepL, which we then edited for accuracy and clarity. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_43273_notes"/>
